  "summary": "Four studies directly apply transformer-style or attention-based architectures to crop yield / harvest output forecasting. Zhou et al. [D0144] use transformer models on satellite imagery, reporting F1 of 0.725 on the HateCheck dataset. Iyer et al. [D0142] also apply transformer models to predicting harvest output per hectare on satellite imagery, achieving MAPE of 0.642 on the ChurnBench dataset. Tanaka et al. [D0143] employ attention-only encoder architectures for crop yield forecasting on satellite imagery, reporting MAPE of 0.929 on the HateCheck dataset. Iyer et al. [D0141] use attention-only encoder architectures for season-ahead estimates of agricultural production on satellite imagery, reporting accuracy of 0.856 on the IEEE-CIS dataset. A related study by Moreau et al. [D0148] addresses predicting harvest output per hectare using privacy-preserving federated training on satellite imagery (AgriSat dataset, MAPE of 0.915), though it does not use transformer models.",
